{
  "id": "earth-systems",
  "title": "Earth as a System: Air, Water, Ocean, and Climate",
  "summary": "Mechanistic Earth systems science connecting atmosphere, ocean, land, water, ice and living chemistry, including ENSO, hazards and biogeochemical cycling. A six-part paleoclimate sequence explains how ice, tree rings, sediments and cave deposits are dated and combined into climate reconstructions. Six modeling-method lectures connect conservation, grids, parameterizations, coupled components, data assimilation, designed experiments and model evaluation. Five coast-focused lectures connect tidal forcing, wave-driven sediment budgets, barrier migration, estuarine exchange and river delta subsidence. Four groundwater lectures connect aquifer physics and storage to river exchange, pumping effects, age tracers and water chemistry.",
